  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>What battery group size does my truck need?</h3>
        <p>Heavy-duty trucks most commonly use JIS N150/N200 (models 145G51/190H52) or DIN88/DIN100 batteries depending on the market. North American vehicles use BCI Group 31 (available on request). Confirm the group size on your existing battery or in the vehicle manual.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do heavy-duty trucks use 12V or 24V systems?</h3>
        <p>Most semi trucks and heavy commercial vehicles use 24V systems (two 12V batteries in series); light trucks and pickups use 12V. Check your vehicle specification before ordering.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>How much CCA does a diesel truck battery need?</h3>
        <p>Diesel engines need high CCA. Heavy-duty trucks commonly require 800–1100+ CCA depending on engine size and climate — colder climates need more. Confirm the exact figure in your vehicle manual.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3>Do you offer OEM and private label truck batteries?</h3>
        <p>Yes. DINWEY is the truck-battery brand of Chengguang Power Tech Co., Ltd. (founded 2002), offering OEM and private label programs with custom branding, packaging and specification.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:24px;">
        📚 Looking for technical guidance? Visit the
        <a href="https://docs.dinweysbattery.com/">DINWEY Knowledge Hub</a> for selection
        guides, JIS vs DIN vs BCI standards, CCA and 12V vs 24V documentation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

